  - date: "2026-08-05 07:38:16"
    message: "Implemented and verified the source-first Markdown Entry editor, automatic structured-paste expansion, recoverable project drafts, existing-note editing, GFM preview, formatting tools and shortcuts."
  - date: "2026-08-05 08:20:12"
    message: "Completed the Markdown-native rich writing redesign: Tiptap document canvas by default, exact CodeMirror Source, GFM Preview, floating and selection formatting controls, safe task/table serialization, responsive browser QA, 51 tests, validation, and production build."
  - date: "2026-08-05 09:39:55"
    message: "Added AI Markdown cleanup and structure tools to the ENTRY editor with selection/document scope, strict no-rewrite prompts, review-before-apply, cancellation, provider errors, browser QA, validation, 51 tests, and production build."
  - date: "2026-08-05 09:55:20"
    message: "Implemented and Electron-verified a Gmail-style three-column Fikr Intel workspace: unchanged project sidebar, compact searchable/filterable/sortable note inbox, and persistent selected-note editor with all existing actions and full Markdown editor access. Lint, typecheck, and 51 tests pass."
  - date: "2026-08-05 10:02:08"
    message: "Removed the grid/masonry view control from the Fikr Intel toolbar while retaining list and graph views."
  - date: "2026-08-05 10:17:12"
    message: "Aligned Fikr Studio typography with SaveADay AI: bundled DM Sans for product UI, Newsreader for editorial hierarchy, mono only for code/machine values, enlarged inbox controls and note rows, and visually verified the Electron workspace."
  - date: "2026-08-05 10:18:13"
    message: "Simplified AI Markdown UX by removing the full-screen review overlay and moving direct Format and Clean up actions into the floating editor toolbar with inline progress, errors, stale-edit protection, cancellation, and undo support. Browser QA, 51 tests, validation, and production build passed."
  - date: "2026-08-05 10:25:50"
    message: "Completed high-contrast monochrome light mode: black primary actions, darker secondary text, stronger neutral borders, clearer selected inbox/sidebar rows, grayscale note-type chrome, and preserved dark-mode semantic colors. Lint, TypeScript, 51 tests, and diff checks passed; Electron editor visually inspected without disturbing the user's unsaved note."
  - date: "2026-08-05 10:28:56"
    message: "Correction: restored the original semantic note-type and tag colors in light mode. The monochrome treatment now applies only to interface chrome, surfaces, borders, selections, links, and primary actions. Lint, TypeScript, and diff checks pass."
  - date: "2026-08-05 10:32:37"
    message: "Completed a quieter inbox hierarchy: removed repetitive note-row, search, filter, banner, and header borders; retained only structural column separation; softened selected rows and New Space; simplified tabs and footer; preserved semantic tag colors. Lint, TypeScript, 51 tests, and diff checks passed. Electron screenshot capture was blocked because the Mac locked."
  - date: "2026-08-05 11:09:01"
    message: "Fixed Tiptap Invalid collection of marks for node text: bold,code. Inline code is authoritative at the rich-editor boundary, conflicting emphasis wrappers are normalized outside fenced blocks, and toolbar actions cannot create invalid code-plus-formatting combinations. Added two regression tests; lint, TypeScript, 53 tests, and diff checks pass."
  - date: "2026-08-05 11:21:09"
    message: "Removed the redundant Markdown Preview mode and converted AI Format and Clean up into icon-only floating-toolbar actions. Preserved global theme and semantic tag-color tokens. Browser QA, 53 tests, validation, and production build passed; ADR-013 records the two-mode editor decision."
  - date: "2026-08-05 11:28:18"
    message: "Fixed synthesis null taskModels crash by resolving the active AI route before model selection; validation, 53 tests, and production build passed."
  - date: "2026-08-05 14:11:37"
    message: "Entry now floats as an absolute bottom overlay above the Intel three-column workspace instead of reserving footer space. Only the composer receives pointer events, the columns extend behind it at full height, and undo feedback sits above the panel. Electron visual QA, lint, TypeScript, 53 tests, and diff checks passed."
  - date: "2026-08-05 14:24:04"
    message: "Simplified the inbox/editor hierarchy: Notes and count now share one compact row; search and filters are shorter; Original and Synthesized tabs no longer repeat icons; the inline Quick edit and Expand controls and their editing state were removed; one toolbar Edit action and double-clicking original note content open the full Markdown editor. Electron layout inspected, lint, TypeScript, 53 tests, and diff checks passed."
  - date: "2026-08-05 14:28:14"
    message: "Replaced the persistent Entry composer with a minimal bottom-right plus FAB. The FAB opens the full Markdown editor, adapts to light/dark themes, retains recoverable project-scoped drafts and the global Command-Shift-M shortcut, and shows a subtle draft indicator. Undo feedback returned to the normal bottom center. Electron visual QA, lint, TypeScript, 53 tests, and diff checks passed."
  - date: "2026-08-05 15:07:29"
    message: "Completed world-class visual polish pass for the Intel inbox: constrained editorial reader measure and rhythm, simplified note toolbar and controls, bounded three-column proportions, softened structural borders, improved light/dark contrast, preserved semantic note colors, added accessible icon labels and focus visibility, hid the FAB during transient overlays, and guarded sub-900px layouts. Verified live Electron UI in dark and light modes plus compact desktop width; lint, TypeScript, 53 tests, static production build, and scoped diff checks passed."
  - date: "2026-08-05 20:05:50"
    message: "Implemented creative-director visual system audit across menus, Settings, Connections, Account, Studio, reader, search, insights, graph, About, and secondary surfaces; lint, typecheck, 53 tests, build, and responsive QA passed."
  - date: "2026-08-05 20:08:44"
    message: "Moved Original and Synthesized switching into the note detail toolbar as a compact accessible segmented control; removed the second header row and aligned reader content."
  - date: "2026-08-05 20:11:24"
    message: "Refined Connections list interaction states with rounded neutral row hover, coordinated monochrome actions, clearer supporting text, and keyboard-operable focus behavior."
  - date: "2026-08-05 20:31:04"
    message: "Implemented an app-wide keyboard shortcut system with safe editable-target handling, cross-surface navigation/search/new-entry commands, discoverable menu entry points, and a responsive shortcut reference dialog. Live browser QA passed, along with lint, TypeScript, 53 tests, diff-check, and production build."
  - date: "2026-08-05 20:44:57"
    message: "Added explicit Cmd/Ctrl+S editor saving while retaining Cmd/Ctrl+Enter, and introduced a restrained app-wide Sonner status system. Save/create/import/export/copy/settings/generation/undo outcomes now share one toast language, storage failures are deduplicated and actionable, and the toaster avoids FAB overlap. Live QA, lint, TypeScript, 53 tests, diff-check, and production build passed."
  - date: "2026-08-06 05:57:00"
    message: "Built and verified isolated ad-hoc-signed Fikr Studio 0.1.20 ARM64 QA app, DMG, and ZIP. Not publishable: history secret scan and npm audit failed, and Developer ID notarization was unavailable."
  - date: "2026-08-06 06:13:55"
    message: "Hardened Studio MCP and relay runtime with ID-token refresh propagation, bounded polling, lease acknowledgements, and synthesized-note idempotency; lint, typecheck, 54 tests, and build pass."
  - date: "2026-08-06 06:14:34"
    message: "Fixed the ad-hoc local-QA package launch crash without changing production signing: main app and Electron helpers receive temporary local-only library-validation entitlements; final package rendered successfully."
  - date: "2026-08-06 06:19:54"
    message: "Fixed update install lifecycle and error recovery: flush storage/cookies before quitAndInstall, reset quit state on failure, and explain signature mismatches. Installed ad-hoc 0.1.20 app was inspected live at the update-ready dialog."
